  "response": "## 1) Severity: CRITICAL | Type: Security\nConsensus: 3/3 reviewers\nTitle: Sanitize imported HTML before storing and rendering it as raw_html\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/post.rb:131-133\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:22\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:36\n- app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb:35-36\n- app/views/embed/best.html.erb:19\n\nExplanation:\nWhen `cook_method == raw_html`, `Post#cook` returns `raw` unchanged. This skips the entire cooking and sanitization pipeline. The result is rendered unescaped in two places:\n- the forum itself;\n- the embed view, via `raw post.cooked`.\n\nThe two import paths are both unsafe:\n- **RSS path:** content goes through `CGI.unescapeHTML` and is stored verbatim. It has no filtering at all.\n- **Readability path:** it whitelists tags but keeps `href`/`src`, so `javascript:` URLs survive.\n\nAnyone who controls the feed or the embedded site's pages can inject `<script>`, `on*` handlers, iframes or similar into the Discourse origin. That is stored XSS.\n\nBecause `raw_html` is a generic cook mode, any future caller that uses it inherits the same hole. Run every imported fragment through a whitelist sanitizer that also rejects non-http(s) schemes.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\n# post.rb\nreturn Sanitize.clean(raw, Sanitize::Config::RELAXED) if cook_method == Post.cook_methods[:raw_html]\n\n# or, in topic_embed.rb before storing\nraw = Sanitize.clean(absolutize_urls(url, contents), Sanitize::Config::RELAXED)\n~~~\n\n## 2) Severity: HIGH | Type: Security\nConsensus: 3/3 reviewers\nTitle: Escape the embed URL before interpolating it into the \"Imported from\" footer\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:13\n\nExplanation:\n`url` is interpolated into `<a href='#{url}'>#{url}</a>` without escaping, and the post is rendered as raw HTML.\n\n`url` can come from `embed_url` in `EmbedController#best`. That request is gated only by a forgeable `Referer` header and a host check. A URL such as `http://embeddable-host/post?x='onmouseover='alert(document.cookie)` passes both:\n- the `/^https?:\\/\\//` check;\n- the `URI(...).host` check.\n\nMany sites return 200 for unknown query strings, so the fetch succeeds. An unauthenticated request therefore produces stored XSS on the forum.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nsafe_url = ERB::Util.html_escape(url)\ncontents = contents + \"\\n<hr>\\n<small>#{I18n.t('embed.imported_from', link: \"<a href='#{safe_url}'>#{safe_url}</a>\")}</small>\\n\"\n~~~\n\n## 3) Severity: HIGH | Type: Security\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Normalize embed_url and rate-limit to prevent unbounded topic creation\n\nAffected:\n- app/controllers/embed_controller.rb:9-17\n- app/controllers/embed_controller.rb:26\n- lib/topic_retriever.rb:14-19\n- lib/topic_retriever.rb:26-30\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:15-30\n\nExplanation:\nThe only check on `embed_url` is that its host matches. Any non-browser client can set the Referer header, so that gate does not stop scripted requests.\n\nEvery distinct string becomes its own `TopicEmbed`, topic and post, all created as `embed_by_username`. Variants such as `?a=1`, `?a=2` or `#x` each count as new. The throttle is keyed on the full URL, so these variants bypass it too.\n\nAn attacker can therefore:\n- mass-create spam topics;\n- grow the DB without bound;\n- force outbound fetches. When feed polling is enabled, each fetch also triggers a full feed poll.\n\nFix:\n- Canonicalize the URL by stripping the query and fragment.\n- Add per-IP rate limiting.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nuri = URI(embed_url); uri.query = nil; uri.fragment = nil\nembed_url = uri.to_s\nRateLimiter.new(nil, \"embed-retrieve-#{request.remote_ip}\", 10, 1.minute).performed!\n~~~\n\n## 4) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 3/3 reviewers\nTitle: Handle the unique-index race when concurrent imports create the same embed\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:15-30\n\nExplanation:\nThe existence check `where(embed_url:).first` runs outside the transaction, so this is a check-then-insert race. Two imports of the same URL can run concurrently, for example:\n- the hourly PollFeed job and a RetrieveTopic job, which calls PollFeed inline;\n- multiple RetrieveTopic jobs, since staff bypass the throttle.\n\nBoth can pass the check. The second `create!` then raises `ActiveRecord::RecordNotUnique`, which fails the job and aborts the rest of the feed loop.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nbegin\n  Topic.transaction do\n    # ... create post + embed\n  end\nrescue ActiveRecord::RecordNotUnique\n  post = TopicEmbed.where(embed_url: url).first.try(:post)\nend\n~~~\n\n## 5) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 3/3 reviewers\nTitle: Handle feed items without content and isolate per-item failures\n\nAffected:\n- app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb:31-37\n\nExplanation:\nMany RSS feeds only provide `<description>`. For those items `i.content` is nil, and `nil.scrub` raises `NoMethodError`.\n\nThe job has `retry: false` and no rescue, so one such item aborts the loop. Every later item is then skipped on every poll. `TopicRetriever` runs this job inline, so retrieval breaks too.\n\n`CGI` is also used without `require 'cgi'`.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nrequire 'cgi'\n...\nrss.items.each do |i|\n  begin\n    raw = i.content || i.description\n    next if raw.blank?\n    content = CGI.unescapeHTML(raw.scrub)\n    TopicEmbed.import(user, url, i.title, content)\n  rescue => e\n    Rails.logger.warn(\"PollFeed item failed: #{e}\")\n  end\nend\n~~~\n\n## 6) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Handle protocol-relative URLs and default ports in absolutize_urls\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:56-73\n\nExplanation:\nTwo separate problems:\n- **Protocol-relative URLs:** `start_with?('/')` also matches `//cdn.example.com/x.png`. That URL is rewritten to `http://host/cdn.example.com/x.png`, breaking CDN links and images.\n- **Port handling:** the check compares against both 80 and 443 regardless of scheme. For example, `http://host:443` loses its port.\n\nThe `a` and `img` loops are also duplicated logic.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nprefix << \":#{uri.port}\" if uri.port != uri.default_port\n...\nif v.start_with?('//')\n  node[attr] = \"#{uri.scheme}:#{v}\"\nelsif v.start_with?('/')\n  node[attr] = \"#{prefix}#{v}\"\nend\n~~~\n\n## 7) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Performance\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Throttle before enqueueing retrieve_topic jobs\n\nAffected:\n- app/controllers/embed_controller.rb:12-17\n- app/views/embed/loading.html.erb:6-12\n\nExplanation:\nEvery request for an unknown URL enqueues a job unconditionally. The loading page also reloads itself every 30s.\n\nAs a result, each open tab enqueues a job every 30s for as long as the topic is missing. That continues indefinitely if the import fails. The 60s throttle is only checked inside the job, so it does nothing to limit the queue.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nkey = \"embed-enqueued:#{Digest::SHA1.hexdigest(embed_url)}\"\nif $redis.set(key, \"1\", nx: true, ex: 60)\n  Jobs.enqueue(:retrieve_topic, user_id: current_user.try(:id), embed_url: embed_url)\nend\nrender 'loading'\n~~~\n\n## 8) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Performance\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Avoid synchronously polling the whole feed for every unknown URL\n\nAffected:\n- lib/topic_retriever.rb:39-43\n\nExplanation:\n`Jobs::PollFeed.new.execute({})` runs inline every time an unknown URL is requested. Each call does the following:\n- downloads and parses the entire feed;\n- runs an import for every item.\n\nThis couples the retriever to the internals of a scheduled job. Combined with the throttle bypass, it also lets an attacker force continuous feed re-processing.\n\nFix:\n- Extract the feed import into a reusable service.\n- Rate-limit polling globally.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nif SiteSetting.feed_polling_enabled?\n  if $redis.set(\"feed-polled-recently\", \"1\", nx: true, ex: 5.minutes.to_i)\n    Jobs::PollFeed.new.execute({})\n  end\n  return if TopicEmbed.where(embed_url: @embed_url).exists?\nend\n~~~\n\n## 9) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Maintainability\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Do not edit an existing migration or use force: true in migrations\n\nAffected:\n- db/migrate/20131223171005_create_top_topics.rb:3\n- db/migrate/20131217174004_create_topic_embeds.rb:3\n\nExplanation:\nAdding `force: true` to the already-shipped `create_top_topics` migration causes two problems:\n- Environments that already ran it never see the change, so schemas diverge.\n- Re-running it silently drops the table and its data.\n\n`force: true` on the new `topic_embeds` migration hides schema conflicts and carries the same data-loss risk. The whitespace edits to `20131210181901_migrate_word_counts.rb` are unrelated churn.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\ncreate_table :top_topics do |t|\n...\ncreate_table :topic_embeds do |t|\n~~~\n\n## 10) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Preserve Disqus category/created_at and handle fetch errors\n\nAffected:\n- lib/tasks/disqus.thor:114-148\n\nExplanation:\nSwitching the task to `import_remote` changes its behavior in three ways:\n- **Removed option:** `--category` is gone, so existing scripts that pass `-c` fail.\n- **Lost dates:** the original `created_at` is dropped, so imported threads get the current timestamp.\n- **New network dependency:** the import now hits the network. Any `OpenURI::HTTPError` (e.g. an old link returning 404) aborts the whole import.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nbegin\n  post = TopicEmbed.import_remote(user, t[:link], title: t[:title],\n                                  category: category_id, created_at: Date.parse(t[:created_at]))\nrescue OpenURI::HTTPError, SocketError => e\n  puts \"Skipping #{t[:link]}: #{e}\"\n  next\nend\n~~~\n\n## 11) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Security\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Avoid Kernel#open on configurable/remote URLs\n\nAffected:\n- app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb:29\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:48\n\nExplanation:\nWith open-uri loaded, `Kernel#open` executes a shell command when its argument starts with `|`. Both call sites pass values that are not fully trusted:\n- `feed_polling_url` is an admin-editable setting, so an admin can run commands on the server.\n- `import_remote` receives URLs from callers, including the Disqus task, without validation.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nSimpleRSS.parse URI.parse(SiteSetting.feed_polling_url).open\nReadability::Document.new(URI.parse(url).open.read, ...)\n~~~\n\n## 12) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Performance\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Add timeouts and a size cap to outbound HTTP fetches\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:48\n- app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb:29\n\nExplanation:\nBoth fetches use open-uri with no explicit timeouts and no size limit, and `import_remote` reads the whole body into memory. A slow or huge response can tie up Sidekiq workers and bloat memory. These fetches are reachable from user requests.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nbody = URI.parse(url).open(open_timeout: 5, read_timeout: 10).read(2.megabytes + 1)\nraise \"Response too large\" if body.bytesize > 2.megabytes\n~~~\n\n## 13) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Performance\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Use feed_key for conditional GET or remove it\n\nAffected:\n- app/jobs/scheduled/poll_feed.rb:20-37\n\nExplanation:\n`feed_key` is defined but never used. As written, every poll does the following:\n- re-downloads the full feed;\n- runs one query per item (N+1);\n- hashes every item's content.\n\nFix:\n- Store Last-Modified/ETag under `feed_key` and skip processing on a 304.\n- Preload existing embeds in a single query.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nheaders = {}\nlm = $redis.get(feed_key)\nheaders['If-Modified-Since'] = lm if lm\nbegin\n  io = open(SiteSetting.feed_polling_url, headers)\nrescue OpenURI::HTTPError => e\n  return if e.io.status[0] == '304'\n  raise\nend\n$redis.set(feed_key, io.meta['last-modified']) if io.meta['last-modified']\n~~~\n\n## 14) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Test\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Align controller spec with job enqueueing behavior\n\nAffected:\n- spec/controllers/embed_controller_spec.rb:40-46\n\nExplanation:\nThe spec expects `TopicRetriever.new(...).retrieve` to be called directly. The controller actually calls `Jobs.enqueue(:retrieve_topic, ...)`.\n\nThe spec therefore only passes if jobs run inline in tests, and it is tied to the wrong layer. It should assert that the job is enqueued.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nJobs.expects(:enqueue).with(:retrieve_topic, has_entry(embed_url: embed_url))\nget :best, embed_url: embed_url\n~~~\n\n## 15) Severity: LOW | Type: Security\nConsensus: 3/3 reviewers\nTitle: Use exact origin comparison in postMessage handler\n\nAffected:\n- app/assets/javascripts/embed.js:17\n\nExplanation:\n`discourseUrl.indexOf(e.origin) === -1` is a substring check, not an equality check. An origin like `https://forum.example.co` passes when `discourseUrl` is `https://forum.example.com/`. Today the impact is limited to resizing the iframe.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~js\nvar a = document.createElement('a'); a.href = discourseUrl;\nvar expectedOrigin = a.protocol + '//' + a.host;\nif (e.origin !== expectedOrigin) { return; }\n~~~\n\n## 16) Severity: LOW | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 2/3 reviewers\nTitle: Replace `end if` with `end` in the embed view\n\nAffected:\n- app/views/embed/best.html.erb:2-8\n\nExplanation:\n`<%- end if %>` turns the next emitted ERB statement into the condition of a trailing `if` modifier. That statement is the logo `link_to` buffer append, so the whole if/else block is conditional on it. The template only works because the append returns a truthy value, which is fragile and confusing.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~erb\n<%- end %>\n~~~\n\n## 17) Severity: LOW | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Make throttle key set-and-expire atomic\n\nAffected:\n- lib/topic_retriever.rb:27-30\n\nExplanation:\n`setnx` followed by a separate `expire` is not atomic. If the process fails between the two calls, the key never expires. That URL is then treated as \"retrieved recently\" forever and is never fetched.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nreturn false if $redis.set(retrieved_key, \"1\", nx: true, ex: 60)\ntrue\n~~~\n\n## 18) Severity: LOW | Type: Bug\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Guard against a missing post when updating an existing embed\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:32-37\n\nExplanation:\nIf the embedded post was hard-deleted, `embed.post` is nil and `PostRevisor.new(nil).revise!` raises. That aborts the feed poll for every remaining item.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\npost = embed.post\nreturn nil if post.blank?\n~~~\n\n## 19) Severity: LOW | Type: Maintainability\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Avoid mutating the caller's contents argument\n\nAffected:\n- app/models/topic_embed.rb:13\n\nExplanation:\n`contents << ...` mutates the string the caller passed in. Callers that reuse the string see the footer appended, and a frozen string raises an error. Build a new string instead.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\ncontents = contents + \"\\n<hr>\\n<small>...</small>\\n\"\n~~~\n\n## 20) Severity: LOW | Type: Maintainability\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Remove dead code and unused keys\n\nAffected:\n- app/jobs/regular/retrieve_topic.rb:1\n- config/locales/server.en.yml:37\n- db/migrate/20131219203905_add_cook_method_to_posts.rb:3\n\nExplanation:\n- `require_dependency 'email/sender'` is unused.\n- The `embed.permalink` locale key is never referenced.\n- The migration's `default: 1` silently couples to `Post.cook_methods[:regular]`; document that.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\n# remove require_dependency 'email/sender'; drop embed.permalink\nadd_column :posts, :cook_method, :integer, default: 1, null: false # 1 == Post.cook_methods[:regular]\n~~~\n\n## 21) Severity: LOW | Type: Test\nConsensus: 1/3 reviewers\nTitle: Make PollFeed guard specs isolate each condition\n\nAffected:\n- spec/jobs/poll_feed_spec.rb:18-28\n\nExplanation:\n`feed_polling_enabled` defaults to false. The `feed_polling_url` and `embed_by_username` specs therefore pass even if those guards are removed. Enable the other conditions so that each spec tests exactly one missing condition.\n\nProposed fix:\n~~~ruby\nbefore do\n  SiteSetting.stubs(:feed_polling_enabled?).returns(true)\n  SiteSetting.stubs(:feed_polling_url).returns(url)\n  SiteSetting.stubs(:embed_by_username).returns(embed_by_username)\nend\n~~~\n",
